{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfzy4SyeBwXZtRihsbEqX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Under the Meridian Works policy files, a $900 routine airfare purchase on October 12, 2026 needs **two approvals before the purchase**:\n\n1. **Manager approval.** The purchase date is after July 1, 2025, so the current $2,500 limit applies (AMD-2). $900 is under that limit, so manager approval is required (EXP-1).\n2. **Travel-office approval.** Airfare above $800 needs advance travel-office approval (TRV-1), and $900 is above $800.\n\n**Finance approval is not needed.** It only applies to routine purchases above $2,500 (EXP-2). The old $2,000 limit (AMD-1) only covered purchases before July 1, 2025, and $900 would be under it anyway.\n\n**Why the expense limits apply to airfare.** EXP-1 and EXP-2 say \"non-travel purchase.\" But EXP-3 says airfare is also subject to \"the relevant purchase approval threshold.\" TRV-2 says all travel expenses are, and that travel-office approval never replaces manager approval. So the airfare needs manager approval as well as travel-office approval.\n\n**What could change this:**\n- **Emergency rule:** It doesn't apply. The purchase is routine, and an emergency would only waive finance approval anyway. It never waives manager or travel-office approval (EMG-1).\n- **Vendor:** No vendor is named. If the airline were a prohibited vendor, the purchase couldn't go ahead without written authorization from the compliance officer (VEN-1)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2473,"cache_read_input_tokens":5564,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2473},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ddebc4dd-db9